## Google Ads WoW Spend — Last Week vs Prior Week

**Windows (complete through 2026-10-30 anchor):** last week 2026-10-24 → 10-30; prior week 2026-10-17 → 10-23. Source: ad platform (fixture).

| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $5,377.43 | $8,029.35 | **+$2,651.92 (+49.3%)** |
| Conversions | 28 | 42 | +14 (+50.0%) |
| CPA | $192.05 | $191.18 | −$0.87 (−0.5%) |

**Read:** Spend jumped +49.3% WoW, and conversions scaled in near lockstep (+50.0%), leaving CPA essentially flat ($192.05 → $191.18). That pattern points to **deliberately increased budget/pace rather than efficiency decay** — the extra dollars bought roughly the same cost-per-conversion as before, not worse.

**Caveats:**
- **No granular driver visible.** My tooling gives platform-level totals only — I can't confirm *which* campaigns, ad groups, or keywords absorbed the +$2,652, or whether a budget change was made intentionally. If no one raised budgets last week, that's worth investigating before assuming it's planned scaling.
- **Conversion volume is small** (28 → 42). At ~40/week, CPA is noisy week to week; the flat CPA is reassuring but not high-confidence.
- **Attribution lag:** conversions in the last week's tail (10-29/10-30) may still be settling, which can understate last-week conversions slightly — though that would only bias CPA higher, and it's already flat.
- Spend is the top-line mover but not a performance verdict — CPA held, so there's no case to pull back based on this week alone.

